This file defines the **autonomous Measure workflow** — instructions for unattended agent runs that cycle through tracks automatically.

**Key sections:**

1. **Load Context** — Read `tracks.md`, `tech-debt.md`, `lessons-learned.md`, and optional `current_directive.md`
2. **Workspace & Progress** — Commit dirty state, finish in-progress phases, or create new tracks from directives/tech-debt
3. **Functionality Review (mandatory)** — Before new work: start dev server, use browser-harness to verify the previous phase actually renders and works, fix anything broken
4. **Implement with TDD** — Red-Green-Refactor, with test/build/smoke-test gates after each task
5. **Verify (mandatory)** — Full test suite, build, app launch, core journey, phase feature, console errors, screenshot check
6. **Finalize** — Enforce 50-line limits on memory files, update tech-debt/lessons-learned, commit with model name

**Critical rules:**
- Auto-answer "yes" to proceed prompts, pick first option when asked what to do next
- Never mark work complete if the app is broken or doesn't launch
- Tests passing ≠ feature working; must verify in real browser
- Never start new work on top of broken functionality
